const content="<article class=\"sn-page\" data-editorial-version=\"4\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine \u00b7 Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/acebeam/logo.png\" alt=\"Acebeam logo\" width=\"293\" height=\"48\" loading=\"lazy\"><h1>Acebeam torches for reading the numbers on a marine diesel</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">Ordering a spare part often starts with a photograph of a plate you can barely see. The overhead light catches the edge of the engine, your phone throws a shadow over the number, and the parts desk still needs the last digit. Acebeam makes compact handheld torches and headlamps. A separate light lets you choose the angle of illumination independently of the camera.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/acebeam/photo.webp\" alt=\"Torches and headlamps from Acebeam\" width=\"500\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\"><section><h2>Read the plate before calling the dealer</h2><p>With the engine stopped and safe to inspect, try holding a low beam across the lettering from one side. On a shiny plate, moving the light a few centimetres can reveal more than increasing the brightness. Ask a second person to take the photograph. Keep the wide shot showing where the plate sits as well as the close-up; both can be useful when the engineer asks which component you mean.</p></section><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/acebeam/detail.webp\" alt=\"Acebeam everyday carry torches\" width=\"500\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\"><section><h2>Leave both hands for the locker</h2><p>An Acebeam headlamp suits a different job: finding the right spare among filters, belts and manuals in a dim cockpit locker. Compare how evenly it lights a page at arm&#x27;s length. We like a manageable low setting for this because white fibreglass and glossy packaging can reflect a powerful beam straight back.</p><p>When contacting Acebeam, describe where you need to see, how long you work at that distance and where the light can recharge. Choose and store the torch before the cabin circuit is isolated for a service. It&#x27;s a small piece of independent equipment that can make a conversation with the mechanic much more productive.</p></section><p><a rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.acebeam.com/\">Compare Acebeam headlamps and torches \u2197</a></p></div></article>";
